\f0\b\fs48 \cf0 A Shot out of the Blue
\f1\b0\fs24 \
\pard\pardeftab720\ri-6019\sl360\slmult1\sa160\qc\partightenfactor0

\f2 \cf0 2 to 3 weeks after Bombing
\f1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\ri-6019\sl360\slmult1\sa160\partightenfactor0

\f2 \cf0 \'93Girlfriend?\'94 Sarah yelling so loud, a shock wave slammed into the line-up, knocking their off hats clean off. \'93Well if she\'92s my girlfriend, she can get the promotion.\'94 Without warning and with blinding speed she pulled out her pistol, shooting Cracker in the chest, high and to the right. Sarah met him at the ground where he lay motionless. Sarah stood up with hands bloodied and stared down the row of men, all of whom now well acquainted with shock and awe. \'93Yes, she gets the promotion.\'94
\f1 \

\f2 \'93Fucking hard core, sweetheart.\'94 The Senior Sergeant blurted out before walking up to Cracker\'92s body and putting another two shots in the stomach and went to put one in the head when Sarah knocked him flying with a short push, sending the shot wide of its target. 
\f1 \

\f2 \'93I want him identifiable.\'94 Sarah stood over the crumpled three-striper and helped him to his feet. \'93I think he has enough holes in him.\'94
\f1 \

\f2 \'93Okay fellas, the prize has been claimed. The ladies can take clean-up duty. Firing Squad dismissed!\'94 
\f1 \

\f2 \'93Oh man! I really needed the extra money.\'94 The constable did have reason to complain. He was expecting his third child and this time he was pretty sure it was his.
\f1 \

\f2 \'93Yeah, fuck this.\'94 Said another Constable. She too had fair grounds for complaint. She was expecting to shoot someone and didn\'92t get to. 
\f1 \

\f2 Hayley and Sarah watched them march off and disappear into the sprawling set of buildings and car-parks of Police Headquarters. Hayley was neutral, inhumanly blank and lost for words.
\f1 \

\f2 \'93Can you arrange a Coroner\'92s Wagon?\'94 Cool and detached, Sarah took Cracker\'92s wrist. \'93No pulse.\'94
\f1 \

\f2 \'93Yes, it\'92s not exactly procedure, but I have never had to clean up after an execution before.\'94 Still shell shocked, but surprisingly lucid, Hayley called it in. The meat-wagon pulled up quickly, the driver explaining they had been \'91put on standby\'92 and had been waiting around the corner for an hour.
\f1 \

\f2 \'93We have to take him to the HRRZ Public Medical Facility Morgue.\'94 Sarah was insistent.
\f1 \

\f2 \'93No, that\'92s way out of our area. The nearest public facility just a couple of k\'92s. Getting through HRRZ security will take hours.\'94 The Driver was adamant.
\f1 \

\f2 \'93I can transfer 10K into your account right now.\'94 Sarah was diplomatic.
\f1 \

\f2 \'93HRRZ it is\'94 The driver was corrupt.
\f1 \

\f2 \'93We are coming along for the ride.\'94 Sarah informed the driver. \'93Let\'92s go Hayley. You wanted a way out, this is our way out.\'94
\f1 \

\f2 \'93You can ride in the back, with your victim.\'94
\f1 \

\f2 \'93Okay. I\'92ll keep him company.\'94
\f1 \

\f2 \'93Try not to shoot anyone else.\'94
\f1 \

\f2 \'93No more shooting people, got it. There are a few more things I need to tell you, but I have to make a few arrangement for our arrival first.\'94 She took out her palm device and made a call.
\f1 \

\f2 Several hours of negotiation at the HRRZ border slowed the journey, but by the time they arrived at the loading-dock of the morgue, it was late and only one attendant was on duty. Even from inside the back of the van, Dr Kathy Logan could be easily heard giggling and flirting with the driver. The rear doors of the van were reefed open flooding the interior with bright sterile light. 
\f1 \

\f2 \'93Okay, who do we have tonight?\'94 Dr Giggles easily slid the heavy trolley out, wheels slapping to the floor and braces clicking into place. She considered the vague human shape in the body-bag and slowly slid the zipper downward, over Cracker\'92s face, down his chest, stopping at the groin, where the zipper seemed to stick. She jerked it up and down furiously before it finally slid free. Spreading the unfastened plastic she made a cursory examination, prodded the wounds and chuckled, \'93You know, I think he might be dead.\'94 
\f1 \

\f2 \'93Thanks Doctor, just sign the pad, certify life extinct.\'94 He handed her his scratched and dented old notepad which was duly signed. \'93Ladies, the next time you need a body moved, I am your man. The One-after-the-one is coming. Ha, Ha.\'94 And he was gone.
\f1 \

\f2 \'93Dawks are everywhere now.\'94 Dr Logan did not find it funny.
\f1 \

\f2 \'93I can only say sorry so many times.\'94 Cracker croaked from the death trolley. \'93Oh, gimme some pain killers, fast.\'94
\f1 \

\f2 \'93Holy mother of consumerism! You\'92re alive.\'94 Delirious and joyful, Hayley hugged Sarah who did not hug back.
\f1 \

\f2 \'93I could not tell you in front of the driver. He will truthfully report a medical practitioner pronounce him dead. When the good doctor here files her report, Cracker will be officially dead.\'94
\f1 \

\f2 MDMA in Dr Kathy\'92s system was starting to fire up again with subtle flushes of warmth washing over her as she hugged Cracker, melting her body around his. He was very tender and coughing up a little blood, but he was in good spirits and healing quickly. \'93Was that zipper really stuck?\'94
\f1 \

\f2 \'93No.\'94 She laughed loudly, kissed him on the cheek and hugged him tighter.
\f1 \

\f2 \'93I nearly cracked a fat.\'94 He hugged her back and winced but took the pain, the hug being so damned good. 
\f1 \

\f2 \'93That was the whole idea.\'94 She did not release him from her embrace, but increased her hold.
\f1 \

\f2 \'93How did you know, Sarah?\'94 Cracker was most interested to know how he was shot three times and managed to survive. Could the stuff from the Gyges disk protect him in such a manner? He doubted it, but what other explanation could there be\cf2 ? \cf0 He remembered the surprise he felt as she turned the gun on him, but the shock had hardly registered when the first pulse from the pistol struck him down. He had often wondered what it felt like to be shot and having had that curiosity satisfied, it was something he would rather not repeat. The concussion of the pulse striking the body was a short prelude to the searing pain of the wound burning and sealing as the projectile drilled its way through his chest, exiting below the shoulder blade. 
\f1 \

\f2 \'93I did not know, but did not have much choice. You were about to be blasted into oblivion by a firing squad.\'94 Sarah was imagining the damage Cracker\'92s body would have sustained from 10 or more shots from a pulse pistol. Chunks of burning flesh, shattered bone and limbs exploding as he fell to the ground. \'93I think it might be the DNA from the disc.\'94 She again lied. 
\f1 \

\f2 \'93You bet my life?\'94
\f1 \

\f2 \'93Yes and you won.\'94 Sarah was not proud of herself, just relieved that her gamble had paid off.
\f1 \

\f2  
\f1 \

\f2 \'93Do you want to see the results of your scans? From last time? Don\'92t get up Cracker, you get the royal treatment.\'94 She kissed him on his bloody cheek and pushed his trolley out the door and towards her lab, Sarah and Hayley following closely behind. The long corridor opened up into a small room with a well fitted out research station. Waving her hand, Dr Logan triggered the holographic emitters into life, the centre of the room was filled with the images of two floating DNA helixes. \'93On the left is the reconstructed DNA strand of Richard Dawkins and next to it is the strand of the clone you are carrying.\'94
\f1 \

\f2 \'93You\'92re pregnant?\'94 Hayley was genuinely surprised, Sarah had said nothing.
\f1 \

\f2 \'93Yes, with a clone. Keep up.\'94 
\f3\i So much for keeping that secret safe,
\f2\i0  Sarah lamented.
\f1 \

\f2 \'93When they are superimposed there is the tiny extra strand of DNA. Zooming in closely on the structure of the double helix you can see the sugar phosphate skeleton is strong and flexible. The base pairs are sturdily attached, the adenine/thymine and cytosine/guanine bonds are smooth and seamless. Now, zooming in on the extra strand and it is clear it is artificial. While the bonds are just as sturdy as human DNA, the structure is not as smooth. I conducted some underground research on it with my military sources. I expended all of my favours to get those guys to divulge the DNA is from a bio-quantum processor. This particular snippet of the code is concerned data storage, specifically compressing data for storage in a suitable biological medium. Cool huh?\'94
\f1 \

\f2  
\f1 \

\f2 \'93Suitable biological medium?\'94 
\f1 \

\f2 \'93Yes, usually a medium filled with artificial cells, sort of like neurons.\'94 Kathy\'92s patch had switched from MDMA to complete clarity and she was presently all business.
\f1 \

\f2 \'93How will it affect real cells and actual neurons of the child?\'94 Sarah could not yet bring herself to think of the foetus as being \'91a baby\'92 or \'91her baby\'92, but \'91the clone\'92 or \'91the child\'92. 
\f1 \

\f2 \'93We cannot know, but if it operates within the body in the manner it does in the processor, the child\'92s brain will be able to store an enormous amount of data. He could brain dump the entirety of human knowledge and perpetually have instantaneous access. He will be a walking data base. That\'92s if it operates in the same manner. I am sure that there are infinite possibilities, most of which do not have a happy ending.\'94
\f1 \

\f2 \'93I really don\'92t know what to do. I have no problem with the concept of termination, but facing the reality is something entirely different.\'94 Sarah fully supported a woman\'92s right to choose, but struggled with the ethics of ending a life merely because of inconvenience or to avoid stagnation of career prospects. If, however, the child was going to be some kind of genetic freak, termination was a very real option, perhaps the only option.
\f1 \

\f2 \'93I can stick a scanning patch to your abdomen and it will transmit data, to me, as the foetus develops. If there are any anomalous developments we can intervene at the earliest possible moment.\'94 
\f1 \

\f2 \'93You would do that for me?\'94 A great weight was lifted from Sarah\'92s shoulders. She could see a way forward.
\f1 \

\f2 \'93Yes, of course.\'94 Kathy Logan was happy to assist.
\f1 \

\f2 \'93Just make sure it\'92s a scanning patch.\'94 
\f1 \

\f2 \'93No hallucinating for you.\'94 Kathy laughed and licked her lips, her tongue drawing in a tiny sample of Cracker\'92s dried blood into her mouth.
\f1 \
}